      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CAJUN (6) resumes. She debuted in the Listed ANZAC Day Stakes at Flemington and whilst well beaten she showed enough there. The camp have Oaks aspirations with her and so kicking of at 1500m with Blake Shinn on board looks ideal. Big watch. BOYS BOUNCE (2) ran a good race on debut at Sandown Lakeside when showing speed in tough conditions, sticking on for a game third. Better for that and will be very hard to run down. GUARDIAN DETECTIVE (8) got home fairly on debut at Bendigo over 1300m and was in the market there. Up in trip should suit and she'll run well. ZOUCITY (5) was big odds on debut at Geelong but ran on well for third. That looks a handy reference, he should be very hard to hold out up in trip. SCAROLE (4) next best.",
